<!--
  Adds the volunteering opt-in to the new-sponsorship flow. The checkbox ends
  up on res.partner.interested_for_volunteering (partner_compassion), which
  is what notifies the volunteer staff of a potential advocate.

  Target:
  - my_compassion.my2_new_sponsorship_details_form — the "Who shall we thank?"
    form of the fast checkout.

  Why there, and not on a wizard step any more:
  the opt-in used to live on the wizard's communication-details step, which
  the fast checkout no longer runs in any flow (see
  new.sponsorship.wizard.STEPS_CONFIGS / _get_step_xmlids: the public flows
  substitute that step, the logged-in flows never listed it). Asking it on the
  checkout page instead would defeat the point of that page, which is to hold
  nothing but what is needed to pay. The details form is asked of exactly the
  audience that used to see the checkbox - public signups, standard and
  Write&Pray alike - only after the payment step rather than before it.

  Consequence, and it is the intended one: the flag now arrives in a write to
  an existing partner instead of in its create() values, which is what finally
  makes partner_compassion's "Potential volunteer" activity fire (it only ever
  looked at write()). See partner_compassion/models/partner_compassion.py.
-->
<odoo>
  <template
    id="new_sponsorship_wizard_volunteering"
    inherit_id="my_compassion.my2_new_sponsorship_details_form"
    name="New Sponsorship Details Volunteering Opt-in"
  >
    <!-- After the optional-address disclosure, so the two required fields
         the form exists for stay at the top and this stays an extra. -->
    <xpath expr="//details" position="after">
      <t t-call="theme_compassion_2025.FormFieldComponent">
        <t t-set="top_class" t-value="'my-3'" />
        <t t-set="label">Volunteering</t>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center">
          <!-- No companion hidden input, unlike the wizard's own checkboxes:
               this form is posted by the browser, not serialized by the
               wizard JS, and a repeated field name would make Odoo read the
               hidden empty value instead of the ticked one. -->
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            id="details_volunteering"
            name="volunteering"
            value="1"
            class="flex-shrink-0"
            t-att-checked="details_prefill.get('volunteering')"
          />
          <label
            class="ms-3 mb-0 body-small bold"
            t-att-for="'details_volunteering'"
          >
                    I wish to volunteer my time (letter translations, events, prayer, ...).
                    Please contact me.
                </label>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-2 p-4 bg-high-eggshell rounded-lg body-small">
                Do you want to inspire other people to sponsor a child?
                Does the situation of children in need particularly touch you and you want to take action?
                <br />
                <br />
                You can volunteer for Compassion and thereby place your talents at the service of the most
                destitute children
                on the planet.
                <br />
                <br />
                Translations, stuffing envelopes, presence at events, being a spokesperson in
                your church or running for the children.
            </div>
      </t>
    </xpath>
  </template>
</odoo>
